WEBVTT

00:33:58.925 --> 00:34:00.587
and about sharing these ideas,

00:34:00.611 --> 00:34:03.774
that even at the moments
where my butterflies come back,

00:34:03.798 --> 00:34:05.806
I'll always say to myself, you know,

00:34:05.830 --> 00:34:09.354
"I'm sure there's one person
at least in this audience

00:34:09.378 --> 00:34:11.946
who will maybe be
a better parent to their child,

00:34:11.970 --> 00:34:14.155
or they're going to be
a better boss at work,

00:34:14.179 --> 00:34:16.418
and so I'm going to do it
for that one person."

00:34:16.442 --> 00:34:20.133
CA: I think that's almost
the number one key to overcoming fear,

00:34:20.157 --> 00:34:22.986
is actually to have something
really important to say.

00:34:23.010 --> 00:34:27.127
Like, if that pulls you through,

00:34:27.151 --> 00:34:29.936
I think that's a crucial part of it.

00:34:29.960 --> 00:34:33.495
So what I'm hearing is,
don't obsess about, like,